1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:05,136
A mining fleet can have enough energy and still miss its
production target.

2
00:00:06,179 --> 00:00:12,057
ElectroDecision compares charging choices and organizes the
evidence needed before an electrification decision.

3
00:00:13,099 --> 00:00:16,958
This video replays outputs from the working calculation
modules.

4
00:00:18,658 --> 00:00:25,251
The case uses four generic underground loaders, a twelve-hour
shift, and a target of seventeen hundred tonnes.

5
00:00:25,909 --> 00:00:28,274
Battery health is eighty-five percent.

6
00:00:28,932 --> 00:00:34,690
The model includes charging losses, critical site demand, and
a ninety-minute charger outage.

7
00:00:35,348 --> 00:00:39,342
These are synthetic assumptions, not measurements from a real
mine.

8
00:00:40,962 --> 00:00:44,131
One charger delivers eleven hundred eighty-eight tonnes.

9
00:00:45,093 --> 00:00:49,462
A second charger on the same supply improves output but still
misses the target.

10
00:00:50,424 --> 00:00:55,697
Adding three hundred fifty kilowatts reaches seventeen hundred
eighty-two tonnes without modeled overload.

11
00:00:56,660 --> 00:01:02,038
Unmanaged charging reaches similar output but overloads supply
for three hundred sixty-nine minutes.

12
00:01:04,158 --> 00:01:07,572
The next shift keeps each vehicle's actual battery energy.

13
00:01:08,730 --> 00:01:13,908
In the upgraded case, a sixty-minute charging break restores
the declared initial charge.

14
00:01:15,066 --> 00:01:18,405
Shift two delivers eighteen hundred seventy-two tonnes.

15
00:01:19,563 --> 00:01:23,842
Two shifts plus the break span twenty-five hours, not a single
day.

16
00:01:25,538 --> 00:01:31,221
A separate evidence workflow filters requirements by
technology, project stage, and jurisdiction.

17
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:37,253
This trolley implementation case starts with twelve open
items, including eight critical items.

18
00:01:37,791 --> 00:01:40,970
A document reference changes declared completeness.

19
00:01:41,508 --> 00:01:45,462
It never verifies contents or certifies regulatory compliance.

20
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:51,934
This is a saved record of a real NVIDIA Nemotron request
through Nebius Token Factory.

21
00:01:53,094 --> 00:01:57,088
The application executed the readiness and project-context
tools.

22
00:01:58,249 --> 00:02:04,681
The model selected evidence identifiers, which the server
validated before building the report from catalog text.

23
00:02:05,842 --> 00:02:10,406
The record contains token usage and tool results, with no
provider key.

24
00:02:11,566 --> 00:02:15,840
It is recorded inference evidence, not a new live request in
this video.

25
00:02:17,541 --> 00:02:24,839
The public repository includes source, an MIT license, setup
instructions, tests, and integration evidence.

26
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:27,609
Operation data is synthetic.

27
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:33,459
Industrial savings, equipment control, and engineering
approval are outside this prototype.

28
00:02:34,609 --> 00:02:36,733
Compare charging choices.

29
00:02:37,342 --> 00:02:40,206
Expose production and supply constraints.

30
00:02:40,815 --> 00:02:43,044
Prioritize missing evidence.

31
00:02:43,653 --> 00:02:47,391
The next step is validation with site data and mining
planners.
